# Copy this file to .dev.vars.staging or .dev.vars.production (one per environment, here in backend/) and fill in the
# values. Those files are git-ignored: never commit values. npm run dev, the db:* and video:hls scripts and
# npm run deploy:<env> read only the vars file of the environment they were told to use (--env).
#
# DATABASE_URL        the Neon connection string (pooled) of THAT environment's own database
# JWT_SIGNING_SECRET  at least 32 random bytes: openssl rand -base64 48
# APPLE_CLIENT_ID     the iOS bundle id, com.somsak.Marauders
# APPLE_TEAM_ID       the 10-character Apple Developer team id (developer.apple.com, Membership details)
# APPLE_KEY_ID        the 10-character id of the Sign in with Apple key (Keys)
# APPLE_PRIVATE_KEY   the text of that key's downloaded AuthKey_<key id>.p8, line breaks written as \n; with the two
#                     names above it lets "Delete Account" revoke the person's Apple grant, and without all three
#                     deleting an Apple account answers 503 (docs/adr/011-account-deletion.md)
# DEV_LOGIN_SECRET    turns on /v1/auth/dev for the Debug app on the Simulator: set it only for the environment the
#                     Debug builds talk to (production while there is one backend, see ADR-010; staging once it exists)
DATABASE_URL=
JWT_SIGNING_SECRET=
APPLE_CLIENT_ID=
APPLE_TEAM_ID=
APPLE_KEY_ID=
APPLE_PRIVATE_KEY=
DEV_LOGIN_SECRET=
